          "end": 43,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:1",
          "start": 21
        },
        "quote": "CONDITIONAL USE PERMIT",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "1a0c1a73-becb-5074-bb4f-bfb72a786bc1",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 510,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:2",
          "start": 45
        },
        "quote": "RESOLUTION introduced by City Manager Dr. Robert M. Perez, in accordance with Section 18.60.010 of the Topeka Municipal Code, approving a Conditional Use Permit to allow for a Short-Term Rental, Type II (non-owner occupied) that is within 500 ft of another Short Term Rental on property located at 1171 SW Medford Avenue and zoned \"R-2\" Single-Family Dwelling District, all being within the City of Topeka, Shawnee County, Kansas. (CU26/02) (Council District No. 6)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "c5e553ef-8d2b-5dc8-b463-db1351171515",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 909,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:3",
          "start": 512
        },
        "quote": "BE IT RESOLVED by the Governing Body of the City of Topeka, Kansas, that the application under the provisions of TMC 18.60.010, approving a Conditional Use Permit to allow for a Short Term Rental Type II that is within 500 ft of another Short Term Rental on property zoned “R-2” Single Family Dwelling District, located at 1171 SW Medford Avenue and more specifically legally described as follows:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "053ae42c-605f-577c-b360-7407e952d56a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 997,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:4",
          "start": 911
        },
        "quote": "WASHBURN PLACE (AMENDED) , Lot 397 AND 399, AND ADJACENT 1/2 VAC ALLEY, MEDFORD AVENUE",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "6495aed8-275e-53cd-bb60-226f8c059966",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1047,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:5",
          "start": 999
        },
        "quote": "be, and the same is hereby approved, subject to:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 6",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 6,
          "component_id": "67bb5b95-44b0-5167-8a37-ad6a53a7cd94",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1189,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:6",
          "start": 1049
        },
        "quote": "Use and development of the site in accordance with the approved Conditional Use Permit (CU26/02) and Statement of Operations from applicant.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:6#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 7",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 7,
          "component_id": "5a13f638-7791-5c45-84fa-0c8d185db610",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1401,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:7",
          "start": 1191
        },
        "quote": "In the event of substantial changes in operations, the applicant shall submit a revised Statement of Operations to the Planning Department to allow staff to ascertain compliance with the Conditional Use Permit.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:7#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 8",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 8,
          "component_id": "172c9c58-6185-5758-9773-d2ec2d770ad7",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2289,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:8",
          "start": 1403
        },
        "quote": "The Conditional Use Permit for the Short Term Rental, Type II shall expire after a period of 24 months from the date of its approval by the Topeka Governing Body or no sooner than July 26, 2026, whichever of these dates occurs last. Kansas House Bill 2481 allows unrestricted operation of a short term rental at the subject address during the period of May 15, 2026 through July 25, 2026. If, upon a written request made by the owner within six months from date of the expiration of the conditional use permit, and after finding that the short term rental has and will continue to comply with all special use requirements for a short term residential rental type II with exception of standard (aa)(1)(ix) regarding its distance from any other short term rental type II, the Planning Director may approve one extension of the conditional use permit not to exceed an additional 24 months.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:8#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 9",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 9,
          "component_id": "bc1a7b7f-4514-5386-9ebc-31f2c812511b",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2373,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:9",
          "start": 2291
        },
        "quote": "ADOPTED AND APPROVED by the Governing Body of the City of Topeka on June 16, 2026.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:9#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
