          "block_index": 17,
          "component_id": "4fecd89f-2047-5c96-aeaa-8b99f79bf269",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2552,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:17",
          "start": 2529
        },
        "quote": "Statement of Operations",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:17#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 18",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 18,
          "component_id": "134e9c27-ee3a-5af0-9fb3-fe23a19410dc",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2632,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:18",
          "start": 2554
        },
        "quote": "Conditional Use Permit for Short Term Rental Type II at 1171 SW Medford Avenue",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:18#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 19",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 19,
          "component_id": "5c2efb5a-3f8f-560c-af5c-7ad51aa54c9a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2850,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:19",
          "start": 2634
        },
        "quote": "The \"Medford House,\" as my family and I call it, has been in our family for roughly 28 years. It has served as my childhood home and a long-term rental property; soon, I hope it will become a short-term rental (STR).",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:19#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 20",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 20,
          "component_id": "89cc2075-8101-541a-9c82-c0069410243b",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3196,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:20",
          "start": 2852
        },
        "quote": "The Medford House offers two bedrooms and one bath for guests to enjoy. While I am new to the STR space and expect a learning experience, I will implement a two-night minimum stay. Trash services will continue to be provided by the City of Topeka. I will also enforce a \"quiet time\" from 10:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m., and no parties will be allowed.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:20#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 21",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 21,
          "component_id": "29125c33-0d04-5d26-a7a7-0c016ee91edc",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3453,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:21",
          "start": 3198
        },
        "quote": "The property will host transient guests with no representative living on-site. However, my goal is not a fully booked schedule every month; I simply want the property to pay for itself while remaining a place I can stay when I return home to visit family.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:21#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "09821 block 22",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 22,
          "component_id": "1fbdb2c8-5f95-5e1c-88e8-0f5102c61aaf",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4238,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:22",
          "start": 3455
        },
        "quote": "Once I move out, the property will be managed by myself and my family. The 2 main points of contact for managing will be my Aunt Pam Metzger (785) 286-2198 and Uncle Ken Metzger (785) 220-4825. The yard and flowers will be on a regular schedule for mowing and watering to ensure the home remains visually appealing. This project is ongoing, and I will continue to improve the property throughout the permitting process and beyond. Over the past 18 months, I have already made significant improvements, including adding new rock to the driveway, remodeling the front and back porches, replacing gutters on the house and garage, and painting the exterior. My goal is for this property to be one of the nicest homes on the street while maintaining the historic feel of the neighborhood.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:resolutions:resolution:09821:block:22#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
